{"base_rate":0.42800528401585203,"brier":0.1086010568031704,"bss":0.5563986043395204,"bss_hi":0.6373268357650241,"bss_lo":0.47620503648538615,"chart":{"base":[617.0,86.9],"fp":[191.2,293.1],"lead":"62,283 272,258.8 482,208.6 692,137.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.56 — higher than 95% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +11pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 99% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 4%; promised 96% → rained 86%"},"rel":"81,448.8 363,322 667.1,94.9"},"country":"NL","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07997357992073982,"ess":352.06705429024544,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Rotterdam</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Rotterdam rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>93%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nROTTERDAM, 4.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.56, ranked 7 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(3&ndash;21) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>216</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>48%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>93%</b></td><td class='num'>227</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Rotterdam</b> <span class=\"muted\">NL</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.56</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>3&ndash;21\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Rotterdam &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Rotterdam\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\"